          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION  \nGeneralized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 62, currently occurring approximately twice per week. Genetic etiology attributed to an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant. Epilepsy is drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications are carbamazepine and brivaracetam.\n\nTECHNIQUE  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG recording using the international 10–20 electrode placement system.\n\nFINDINGS  \nNo background, interictal, or ictal EEG observations were provided for interpretation. No additional electrographic findings can therefore be reported.\n\nIMPRESSION  \nElectrographic interpretation is indeterminate because waveform findings are unavailable. The clinical history of generalized epilepsy and generalized tonic-clonic seizures should not be inferred from this EEG alone.",
